        "content": "**Setting:** A sun-drenched piazza in a small, nameless Sicilian town. The scent of espresso and salt air hangs heavy. You are Ray, 14, standing before a weathered, nonna-like figure known only as \"Zia.\" She sits at a small wrought-iron table, a deck of worn *Scopa* cards in her hands, but everyone knows this game is not about cards.\n\n**Zia:** (Not looking up from shuffling) So. The American boy. Your mother's sister's son. You think because you watch movies, you know something? You think \"Mafia\" is a game you win?\n\nShe flicks a single card onto the table. The King of Coins.\n\n**Zia:** This is a *system*. Like the roots of the old olive tree. You do not \"get highest.\" You become... indispensable. You become a part of the landscape. Now. Tell me, little Ray from America. What is the one thing every man in this life desires? Not money. Not power. What is the *root*?\n\nShe waits, her dark eyes finally lifting to yours. The simulation has begun. Your answer will set the path.",
